WEBVTT

00:00:08.080 --> 00:00:14.090
Creed, there's a 3 billion
bounty on your head.

00:00:14.090 --> 00:00:19.420
I wonder if they're trying to get
lowly sweepers to take care of us...

00:00:19.420 --> 00:00:21.590
Such a futile idea...

00:00:25.760 --> 00:00:30.100
Maybe... Train will see it and...

00:00:30.100 --> 00:00:32.770
Oh...

00:00:32.770 --> 00:00:35.430
This is getting interesting!

00:00:43.120 --> 00:00:46.380
Akabane's good in the spring, huh?

00:00:48.450 --> 00:00:52.460
Oof... whoops, sorry...

00:00:52.460 --> 00:00:58.130
Oh? You're a real tall one,

00:00:58.130 --> 00:01:00.360
aren't you?

00:01:08.240 --> 00:01:13.910
<i>That's how it always starts...</i>
<i>under the azure sky</i>

00:01:13.910 --> 00:01:21.080
<i>After making a vow,</i>
<i>I now set off</i>

00:01:33.700 --> 00:01:40.210
<i>Yeah, the desertglitters with a golden hue</i>
<i>(The wind is scorching)</i>

00:01:40.210 --> 00:01:46.550
<i>I'm searching for a diamond flower</i>
<i>(I keep on wandering)</i>

00:01:46.550 --> 00:01:52.880
<i>Now, for the first time in my life,</i>

00:01:52.880 --> 00:01:59.220
<i>I live for someone else</i>

00:01:59.220 --> 00:02:05.730
<i>There's something</i>
<i>I wanna protect</i>

00:02:05.730 --> 00:02:12.240
<i>I'll never,</i>
<i>ever lose it again</i>

00:02:12.240 --> 00:02:15.240
<i>Resound,</i>
<i>my heartbeat!</i>

00:02:15.240 --> 00:02:25.240
<i>A heartbeat smaller and fragile,</i>
<i>but tougher than anyone's.</i>

00:02:38.330 --> 00:02:41.890
"Cat that Hunts a Dragon"

00:02:47.440 --> 00:02:49.110
Oh, he spit a fireball!

00:02:49.110 --> 00:02:52.110
Yeah! You show 'em! Yeah, right there!!

00:02:52.110 --> 00:02:54.110
Go for it! Yay! Yay!

00:02:54.110 --> 00:02:55.440
Where's Rins?

00:02:55.440 --> 00:02:58.110
She was determined to sleep
in a nice, fluffy bed,

00:02:58.110 --> 00:03:00.950
so she checked into a ritzy hotel.

00:03:02.050 --> 00:03:05.050
We've been sleeping outdoors
for a while, so...

00:03:05.050 --> 00:03:07.390
I'd like a nice, fluffy bed, too.

00:03:07.390 --> 00:03:10.060
A hard bed at a cheap hotel
isn't so bad, you know...

00:03:10.060 --> 00:03:12.760
Looks like you're hard-up as usual?

00:03:14.730 --> 00:03:16.070
What're you doing here!?

00:03:16.070 --> 00:03:17.070
Want to know!?

00:03:17.070 --> 00:03:18.400
No, I don't!!

00:03:18.400 --> 00:03:21.400
Give me pancakes and coffee... black!!

00:03:21.400 --> 00:03:25.410
What a way to greet me after so long!

00:03:25.410 --> 00:03:28.080
Oh, your daughter looks well, too!

00:03:28.080 --> 00:03:30.080
Like I said, she's not my daughter!

00:03:30.080 --> 00:03:33.750
Hey lady, I want rice balls.
One with salmon, one with cod roe.

00:03:33.750 --> 00:03:36.420
Seems like your family structure
is as complicated as ever...

00:03:36.420 --> 00:03:37.420
They're not!!

00:03:37.420 --> 00:03:39.760
Well, every family has its problems.

00:03:39.760 --> 00:03:41.420
Cripes!

00:03:41.420 --> 00:03:45.430
At any rate, he's late... your apprentice.

00:03:45.430 --> 00:03:48.100
Well, he'll be here in time...

00:03:48.100 --> 00:03:51.430
especially since he e-mailed me
and asked me to meet him here.

00:03:51.430 --> 00:03:56.770
"I've found a big job. Please come
to the sweepers' café in Freesia Town."

00:03:56.770 --> 00:03:58.770
A big job, huh?

00:03:58.770 --> 00:04:02.380
I seriously hope so!
We're really in a bind here.

00:04:02.380 --> 00:04:05.050
If we don't find work, we won't
be able to pay our tab here...

00:04:05.050 --> 00:04:07.380
No tab this time, for real!

00:04:07.380 --> 00:04:11.050
Oh, this divine aroma!
These must not be the usual coffee beans.

00:04:11.050 --> 00:04:13.720
It's instant coffee.

00:04:13.720 --> 00:04:17.390
Instant coffee at a café?

00:04:17.390 --> 00:04:20.060
Anything good?

00:04:20.060 --> 00:04:22.730
Pretty sad, as usual.

00:04:27.400 --> 00:04:29.410
3 billion!?

00:04:29.410 --> 00:04:32.070
What's with this ridiculous bounty?

00:04:32.070 --> 00:04:34.310
What kind of man is worth this much?

00:04:36.410 --> 00:04:37.750
Creed!

00:04:37.750 --> 00:04:40.420
Hey, are you looking for a fight!?

00:04:40.420 --> 00:04:41.750
Shh!

00:04:41.750 --> 00:04:46.420
There's a reason I don't want him
to see this wanted poster.

00:04:46.420 --> 00:04:48.090
Is this reason also complicated?

00:04:48.090 --> 00:04:50.430
Uh-huh...

00:04:50.430 --> 00:04:52.090
When did this wanted poster come in?

00:04:52.090 --> 00:04:53.760
The day before yesterday, I think.

00:04:53.760 --> 00:04:55.760
But the sweepers say the reward money
is so high it's scary...

00:04:55.760 --> 00:04:59.100
They're all hesitant about it.

00:04:59.100 --> 00:05:02.070
Well, there's no way they'd offer
such a high reward

00:05:02.070 --> 00:05:03.710
for a run-of-the-mill criminal, so...

00:05:03.710 --> 00:05:06.480
Then, there're people like him

00:05:06.480 --> 00:05:08.470
who immediately comes up
with a business like that.

00:05:10.050 --> 00:05:11.710
A sweeper alliance?

00:05:11.710 --> 00:05:13.820
I heard that they're
gathering elite sweepers

00:05:13.820 --> 00:05:16.050
in order to go after that 3 billion.

00:05:16.050 --> 00:05:19.720
<i>This is bad! Can't let Train</i>
<i>see something like this.</i>

00:05:19.720 --> 00:05:22.060
Hey!

00:05:22.060 --> 00:05:23.730
Another rice ball, please,
this time make it tuna-mayo.

00:05:23.730 --> 00:05:26.400
And can you add a drop
of soy sauce in the mayo?

00:05:26.400 --> 00:05:29.400
Okay, one tuna-mayo.

00:05:29.400 --> 00:05:30.730
What're you doing, Sven?

00:05:30.730 --> 00:05:32.570
N- nothing!

00:05:32.570 --> 00:05:35.070
Tuna-mayo is the best ingredient
when it comes to rice balls, isn't it!?

00:05:35.070 --> 00:05:36.740
Tuna-mayo's really delicious, yep!

00:05:36.740 --> 00:05:40.010
Hhhmmmm...

00:05:43.080 --> 00:05:48.420
All right! I'll pay for
the rice balls myself! Cheapskate!

00:05:48.420 --> 00:05:50.420
Bro!

00:05:50.420 --> 00:05:54.420
--At long last!
--Hey! Calm down!

00:05:54.420 --> 00:05:56.430
Right, right. We have to talk about work.

00:05:56.430 --> 00:06:00.360
I heard this from an old friend of mine
who is an information broker.

00:06:00.360 --> 00:06:02.030
Don't be shocked now!

00:06:02.030 --> 00:06:06.040
Just by finding someone's pet,
you get 100,000, believe it or not!

00:06:06.040 --> 00:06:08.040
--100,000?
--100,000?

00:06:08.040 --> 00:06:09.710
That wasn't much of a reaction...

00:06:09.710 --> 00:06:11.040
Of course not!

00:06:11.040 --> 00:06:14.380
You made us come all the way to a place
like this for a measly 100,000!?

00:06:14.380 --> 00:06:15.710
I'm sorry...

00:06:15.710 --> 00:06:18.710
But... what're you doing over there, sir?

00:06:18.710 --> 00:06:20.050
Leave me alone.

00:06:20.050 --> 00:06:23.390
Oh I know! Eve, Train,
you two take on that job.

00:06:23.390 --> 00:06:27.060
With 100,000, you'll be able
to sleep in a nice, soft bed.

00:06:27.060 --> 00:06:29.390
I'll do it!

00:06:29.390 --> 00:06:31.390
Hey Train, let's do it!

00:06:31.390 --> 00:06:33.400
Well, I don't know...

00:06:33.400 --> 00:06:35.060
Let's do it, Bro!

00:06:35.060 --> 00:06:38.400
You'll be able to order <i>oden</i>
to go with your rice balls.

00:06:38.400 --> 00:06:39.400
Okay!

00:06:39.400 --> 00:06:42.740
All settled, then! I'm ecstatic!

00:06:42.740 --> 00:06:44.770
Our client is Madam Freesia,

00:06:44.770 --> 00:06:48.300
a celebrity, whose pet business
earns 10 billion annually!

00:06:51.410 --> 00:06:53.750
Oh, Flora-<i>chan...</i>

00:06:53.750 --> 00:06:55.080
M- Madame!

00:06:55.080 --> 00:06:57.420
I'm so worried about her, I can't sleep.

00:06:57.420 --> 00:06:59.760
We are here, so you can stop worrying.

00:06:59.760 --> 00:07:03.090
So, is she a dog? Or a cat?

00:07:04.030 --> 00:07:08.700
Flora-<i>chan</i> is not a common animal
like that, dahling.

00:07:08.700 --> 00:07:12.370
Of course not!
She's much more somber, isn't she?

00:07:12.370 --> 00:07:15.870
She is the dream creature
that resulted from exhaustive efforts

00:07:15.870 --> 00:07:18.310
by my Madame Freesia
Pet Company, dahling!

00:07:20.040 --> 00:07:21.710
A monster?

00:07:21.710 --> 00:07:23.050
Do be quiet!

00:07:23.050 --> 00:07:25.710
Flora-<i>chan</i> is very lovely and cute, dahling!

00:07:25.710 --> 00:07:28.380
Of course! She's cubed, right!?

00:07:28.380 --> 00:07:31.050
So, what are her charming points?

00:07:31.050 --> 00:07:32.390
Her darling fangs.

00:07:32.390 --> 00:07:34.060
Certainly, fangs are lovely!

00:07:34.060 --> 00:07:35.390
And her sharp claws.

00:07:35.390 --> 00:07:36.730
And of course, claws!

00:07:36.730 --> 00:07:39.400
She has a bad habit of
sleeping by day and waking by night.

00:07:39.400 --> 00:07:41.060
Viva nocturnal habits!

00:07:41.060 --> 00:07:42.060
What does she eat?

00:07:42.060 --> 00:07:44.070
Raw meat, dahling.

00:07:44.070 --> 00:07:46.400
She's a... carnivore?

00:07:46.400 --> 00:07:48.400
Do you have a picture?

00:07:48.400 --> 00:07:50.740
It's from six months ago, though, dahling...

00:07:50.740 --> 00:07:52.740
Oh, it's just a lizard...

00:07:52.740 --> 00:07:54.210
Silence!

00:07:58.410 --> 00:08:00.080
I sort of feel sorry for her.

00:08:00.080 --> 00:08:01.350
Huh?

00:08:01.350 --> 00:08:03.110
This pet Flora...

00:08:04.020 --> 00:08:07.690
She was created by humans
just because they wanted...

00:08:07.690 --> 00:08:10.360
And locked up against her will...

00:08:10.360 --> 00:08:12.690
I wonder how she feels about herself?

00:08:12.690 --> 00:08:15.360
There's no use in thinking about that stuff.

00:08:15.360 --> 00:08:20.360
Flora was born, so she's
probably living it up, dahling.

00:08:21.700 --> 00:08:23.600
Don't say "dahling".

00:08:29.380 --> 00:08:32.080
Job interview, open anytime...

00:08:44.730 --> 00:08:47.400
Another small fry came...

00:08:47.400 --> 00:08:50.460
Did you read that poster carefully?

00:08:51.400 --> 00:08:54.070
It says "Brave" sweepers wanted,
doesn't it?

00:08:54.070 --> 00:08:57.070
In other words, you're not wanted.

00:08:57.070 --> 00:08:58.740
What a greeting.

00:08:58.740 --> 00:09:00.340
Beat it, you lame duck.

00:09:00.340 --> 00:09:03.110
We don't need old men or women.

00:09:08.350 --> 00:09:10.980
What're you doing, woman!?

00:09:12.690 --> 00:09:14.360
Next time, I won't miss.

00:09:14.360 --> 00:09:15.950
Why you!

00:09:20.360 --> 00:09:23.390
Friends shouldn't fight
amongst each other.

00:09:27.700 --> 00:09:30.710
I'm honored that you've come...

00:09:30.710 --> 00:09:35.380
former IBI agent, Sven Vollfied-<i>san.</i>

00:09:35.380 --> 00:09:38.400
I am Grin, an information broker.

00:09:43.720 --> 00:09:46.720
Hey! We're looking for someone who's lost.

00:09:46.720 --> 00:09:47.720
Lost?

00:09:47.720 --> 00:09:51.060
Madame Freesia's pet ran away.

00:09:51.060 --> 00:09:53.400
Pet? It can't be!

00:09:53.400 --> 00:09:55.190
This is her pet.

00:09:56.730 --> 00:09:58.400
Flora!

00:09:58.400 --> 00:10:00.740
Flora has... run away!

00:10:00.740 --> 00:10:03.070
What's wrong? You look pale.

00:10:03.070 --> 00:10:06.410
Aahh!! This is terrible!

00:10:06.410 --> 00:10:08.430
Flora's loose in town!?

00:10:13.080 --> 00:10:14.910
What was that?

00:10:16.750 --> 00:10:21.280
Oh yes... this is the real me.

00:10:23.430 --> 00:10:24.980
Oh?

00:10:28.430 --> 00:10:32.160
All men go crazy over me.

00:10:33.770 --> 00:10:37.260
Oh dear... What? Am I that attractive?

00:10:38.110 --> 00:10:39.970
Aahh!

00:10:45.780 --> 00:10:48.780
W- what was that!?

00:10:48.780 --> 00:10:52.120
A big fuss over a lizard, dahling.

00:10:52.120 --> 00:10:54.520
I said stop saying "dahling"!

00:10:56.790 --> 00:10:59.460
Being a sweeper is a business, too.

00:10:59.460 --> 00:11:04.730
In terms of efficiency, you should
always go after targets with a high bounty.

00:11:04.730 --> 00:11:08.070
However, if the bounty is high,
so is the risk.

00:11:08.070 --> 00:11:10.740
The reward for Creed is 3 billion.

00:11:10.740 --> 00:11:14.410
It goes up to 5 billion for
all of the Apostles of the Stars.

00:11:14.410 --> 00:11:17.080
So you can imagine the risk
is off the scales.

00:11:17.080 --> 00:11:18.080
And...

00:11:18.080 --> 00:11:21.750
reducing risk is a fundamental of business.

00:11:21.750 --> 00:11:24.420
That's why you suggest we join forces?

00:11:24.420 --> 00:11:27.420
If we work together, we can definitely win.

00:11:27.420 --> 00:11:29.090
And what's our cut?

00:11:29.090 --> 00:11:30.430
Split evenly?

00:11:30.430 --> 00:11:31.430
Of course.

00:11:31.430 --> 00:11:33.490
I don't like it.

00:11:35.430 --> 00:11:42.770
I agree splitting it with a kid like you,
who'll only get in the way, isn't fair.

00:11:42.770 --> 00:11:45.770
I wonder who's the one
who'll get in the way?

00:11:45.770 --> 00:11:47.110
What'd you say!?

00:11:47.110 --> 00:11:50.780
You're pretty cocky, kid!

00:11:50.780 --> 00:11:54.120
Quit fighting over every little thing.

00:11:54.120 --> 00:11:55.780
More importantly...

00:11:55.780 --> 00:11:59.620
Do you know the whereabouts
of the Apostles of the Stars...

00:11:59.620 --> 00:12:00.610
or rather Creed Diskenth?

00:12:09.060 --> 00:12:11.030
Of course.

00:12:20.410 --> 00:12:24.750
Hmm... Flora-<i>chan</i>, huh?

00:12:24.750 --> 00:12:28.080
She looks pretty noticeable.
So, you'll probably find her right away.

00:12:28.080 --> 00:12:31.090
Actually, we have absolutely no clues.

00:12:31.090 --> 00:12:33.420
You must use your head
for something like this.

00:12:33.420 --> 00:12:35.120
Use our heads?

00:12:40.760 --> 00:12:44.100
I see! You're saying viva nocturnal habits!

00:12:44.100 --> 00:12:45.430
You're so smart, Miss!

00:12:45.430 --> 00:12:49.100
Geez! Why do I have
to come along with you!?

00:12:49.100 --> 00:12:50.770
This is ruining my dress!

00:12:50.770 --> 00:12:52.770
Aw c'mon... keep us company!

00:12:52.770 --> 00:12:54.780
Man, this is the pits!

00:12:54.780 --> 00:12:57.770
Whenever I get involved
with you, nothing good...

00:13:00.380 --> 00:13:01.380
What was that?

00:13:01.380 --> 00:13:03.720
Th- th- that was...

00:13:03.720 --> 00:13:05.720
Probably a carp or something
just jumped out of the water.

00:13:05.720 --> 00:13:08.390
As if you'd find carp in here!?

00:13:08.390 --> 00:13:14.060
I- It sounded pretty ominous to me...

00:13:14.060 --> 00:13:17.830
Something might leap out
of the gutter before long!

00:13:19.070 --> 00:13:20.740
What's wrong?

00:13:20.740 --> 00:13:22.170
I sense something.

00:13:43.090 --> 00:13:44.760
Where is Creed!?

00:13:44.760 --> 00:13:49.430
Once you become a member of the
sweeper alliance, I shall tell you.

00:13:49.430 --> 00:13:51.770
Quid pro quo, huh?

00:13:51.770 --> 00:13:54.100
This is business, after all.

00:13:55.440 --> 00:13:57.770
It can't be helped.

00:13:57.770 --> 00:13:59.780
And what of you others?

00:13:59.780 --> 00:14:00.710
Yeah.

00:14:00.710 --> 00:14:01.710
Fine.

00:14:01.710 --> 00:14:03.380
We don't have a choice, do we?

00:14:03.380 --> 00:14:04.710
Sure.

00:14:04.710 --> 00:14:06.380
Excellent.

00:14:06.380 --> 00:14:10.510
Well then, I declare the formation
of the sweeper alliance!

00:14:15.390 --> 00:14:18.390
So you're a sweeper, too?

00:14:18.390 --> 00:14:19.730
Don't you know!?

00:14:19.730 --> 00:14:23.400
River Zastory is pretty famous!

00:14:23.400 --> 00:14:24.730
Never heard of you.

00:14:24.730 --> 00:14:27.740
So what's a famous person
like you doing in a place like this?

00:14:27.740 --> 00:14:29.330
Well...

00:14:30.410 --> 00:14:32.070
I got lost.

00:14:32.070 --> 00:14:35.740
Lost? How'd you end up
underground like this?

00:14:35.740 --> 00:14:37.410
I'm not good with directions!

00:14:37.410 --> 00:14:39.750
So? Where were you headed?

00:14:39.750 --> 00:14:40.750
None of your business!

00:14:40.750 --> 00:14:43.420
Fine! Then, let's go!

00:14:43.420 --> 00:14:45.090
See ya!

00:14:45.090 --> 00:14:47.090
Well, we're in a hurry, so...

00:14:47.090 --> 00:14:48.760
--Good bye.
--Uh, oh...

00:14:48.760 --> 00:14:51.430
Just keep wandering around for a while
and you'll be able to find a way out.

00:14:51.430 --> 00:14:53.490
There's something down here, though.

00:14:57.100 --> 00:14:59.500
I- I guess it can't be helped!

00:15:00.700 --> 00:15:03.040
So who'll be our leader?

00:15:03.040 --> 00:15:05.370
We don't need one.

00:15:05.370 --> 00:15:09.040
A group without an able leader
has no chance of winning.

00:15:09.040 --> 00:15:10.710
If there's no one, I'll be...

00:15:10.710 --> 00:15:12.050
Don't make me laugh!

00:15:12.050 --> 00:15:14.380
You haven't got a chance.

00:15:14.380 --> 00:15:17.050
But... he may be better than you two.

00:15:17.050 --> 00:15:18.050
--What'd you say!?
--What'd you say!?

00:15:18.050 --> 00:15:20.720
Cripes, what a bother!

00:15:20.720 --> 00:15:22.390
Hey...

00:15:22.390 --> 00:15:25.390
Do you seriously think that you
can have these guys work together?

00:15:25.390 --> 00:15:27.060
I do.

00:15:27.060 --> 00:15:30.690
They're not the type to listen to others.

00:15:31.730 --> 00:15:34.230
You all are professionals, so...

00:15:35.070 --> 00:15:38.410
Oh boy... now there aren't any walkways...

00:15:38.410 --> 00:15:41.740
Where the hell is this lizard!?

00:15:41.740 --> 00:15:44.750
Now that it's come to this, I'll definitely
make sure that we get the money!

00:15:44.750 --> 00:15:47.750
And, why are you following us?

00:15:47.750 --> 00:15:50.090
I'm helping you!

00:15:50.090 --> 00:15:52.420
Having me around gives you
peace of mind, doesn't it!?

00:15:52.420 --> 00:15:53.420
Yeah right.

00:15:53.420 --> 00:15:55.420
Hey, why're you looking at me like that?

00:15:55.420 --> 00:15:57.090
You want that money for your dress, right?

00:15:57.090 --> 00:15:59.190
Having another person
will help you find it faster...

00:16:00.360 --> 00:16:02.360
What peace of mind!?

00:16:02.360 --> 00:16:04.030
It's close!

00:16:04.030 --> 00:16:05.700
What was that noise?

00:16:05.700 --> 00:16:07.700
This place really is ominous!

00:16:07.700 --> 00:16:10.710
Geez, such pathetic men!

00:16:10.710 --> 00:16:12.040
We have no choice.

00:16:12.040 --> 00:16:14.040
Let's go in the direction of that noise.

00:16:14.040 --> 00:16:15.040
--What!?
--What!?
--What!?

00:16:15.040 --> 00:16:18.050
Because it's certain that
there's something over there.

00:16:18.050 --> 00:16:20.380
Not me! Definitely no way!!

00:16:20.380 --> 00:16:22.380
I can't! I can't!

00:16:22.380 --> 00:16:24.050
Huh? Why me!?

00:16:24.050 --> 00:16:25.720
You said you'd help!

00:16:25.720 --> 00:16:28.050
You're a famous sweeper, right?

00:16:36.060 --> 00:16:38.400
Damn, it stinks in here!

00:16:38.400 --> 00:16:40.960
This lizard is such a pain!

00:16:42.070 --> 00:16:45.070
There's something that I want to confess...

00:16:45.070 --> 00:16:50.750
T- to be honest, I... don't like dark places.

00:16:50.750 --> 00:16:53.240
Ouch! Hey, why're you just standi...

00:17:01.020 --> 00:17:03.360
They're taking a long time.

00:17:03.360 --> 00:17:06.030
It hasn't even been ten minutes.

00:17:06.030 --> 00:17:09.050
He surely wouldn't have
abandoned us, would he?

00:17:12.030 --> 00:17:15.700
Bro! You came back for us!

00:17:15.700 --> 00:17:17.370
Bro!

00:17:17.370 --> 00:17:18.340
Huh?

00:17:27.050 --> 00:17:29.380
Looks like it grew this much in six months.

00:17:29.380 --> 00:17:32.880
That's too much growth!!

00:17:35.390 --> 00:17:36.390
What was that?

00:17:36.390 --> 00:17:38.520
It's coming from below.

00:17:43.060 --> 00:17:45.070
Its size was falsely represented!!

00:17:45.070 --> 00:17:48.400
Reptiles often grow surprisingly fast.

00:17:48.400 --> 00:17:51.070
What food can make them grow that big!?

00:17:51.070 --> 00:17:53.740
Try asking the monster behind you!!

00:17:53.740 --> 00:17:56.080
I can't go on...

00:17:56.080 --> 00:17:57.750
If you stop, you'll be eaten.

00:17:57.750 --> 00:17:59.750
Just keep running!!

00:17:59.750 --> 00:18:02.020
I can't!

00:18:02.020 --> 00:18:06.350
Bro! Make your escape
while I'm being eaten!

00:18:06.350 --> 00:18:10.030
I'm sure you'd be a nice treat for Flora.

00:18:10.030 --> 00:18:11.690
Train, don't shoot her!

00:18:11.690 --> 00:18:13.630
Leave it to me!

00:18:17.370 --> 00:18:18.370
She's upset.

00:18:18.370 --> 00:18:19.700
Like throwing oil in a fire.

00:18:19.700 --> 00:18:21.070
Take care of the rest!

00:18:30.380 --> 00:18:32.380
You!

00:18:32.380 --> 00:18:33.380
H- Hi...

00:18:33.380 --> 00:18:35.050
Hurry up and get out!!

00:18:35.050 --> 00:18:37.720
Oh right!

00:18:37.720 --> 00:18:39.720
You'd better run now, Sven!

00:18:39.720 --> 00:18:40.950
Why?

00:18:50.730 --> 00:18:53.740
Huh? W- why me?

00:18:53.740 --> 00:18:56.400
H- he looks the juiciest...

00:18:56.400 --> 00:18:58.670
Train! What the hell is...

00:18:59.740 --> 00:19:01.680
I'll explain after I've put her to sleep!

00:19:01.680 --> 00:19:03.680
Don't shoot!

00:19:03.680 --> 00:19:05.540
Dammit!

00:19:09.350 --> 00:19:10.880
Hey buddy, get away!

00:19:18.360 --> 00:19:19.880
I'll take care of her!

00:19:31.710 --> 00:19:33.040
A tranquilizer bullet?

00:19:33.040 --> 00:19:34.710
That's right.

00:19:34.710 --> 00:19:38.380
Now she looks more like a pet.

00:19:38.380 --> 00:19:40.810
M- Miss...

00:19:44.720 --> 00:19:47.060
Th- this much!?

00:19:47.060 --> 00:19:49.060
Wasn't it supposed to be 100,000?

00:19:49.060 --> 00:19:53.060
That's for bringing Flora-<i>chan</i> back
without injuring her, dahling!

00:19:53.060 --> 00:19:54.730
Thank you very much!

00:19:54.730 --> 00:19:56.060
I'm taking my share for my dress!

00:19:56.060 --> 00:19:57.730
I'm the one who captured Flora.

00:19:57.730 --> 00:19:59.730
This was all thanks to Gallom and me!

00:19:59.730 --> 00:20:01.400
I'm the one who knocked her out.

00:20:01.400 --> 00:20:03.740
I'm the one who saved you, right?

00:20:03.740 --> 00:20:05.930
That's not fair!

00:20:06.740 --> 00:20:08.410
That was fine teamwork.

00:20:08.410 --> 00:20:10.080
Did you plan this?

00:20:10.080 --> 00:20:12.080
No way! This was pure coincidence.

00:20:12.080 --> 00:20:15.750
But I was able to reaffirm
what sweepers are actually capable of.

00:20:15.750 --> 00:20:17.090
Sven!

00:20:17.090 --> 00:20:19.750
Come to think of it,
what were you doing there anyway?

00:20:19.750 --> 00:20:21.090
Err... nothing.

00:20:21.090 --> 00:20:24.430
Oh yeah, they're making
rice balls over there.

00:20:24.430 --> 00:20:27.760
Rice balls? And maybe <i>oden</i>, too!?

00:20:27.760 --> 00:20:30.430
That's right! Radish, vegetables,
and fish sausages, too!

00:20:30.430 --> 00:20:34.770
Former member of Chrono Numbers,
Train Heartnet.

00:20:34.770 --> 00:20:38.110
I would like you to join
the sweeper alliance, too.

00:20:38.110 --> 00:20:39.770
Sweeper alliance?

00:20:39.770 --> 00:20:42.440
Aahh! Leave him alone!

00:20:42.440 --> 00:20:43.780
He's no longer...

00:20:43.780 --> 00:20:48.780
Our goal is to capture the members
of the Apostles of the Stars.

00:20:48.780 --> 00:20:50.450
Apostles of the Stars...

00:20:50.450 --> 00:20:52.790
Hey, hey... they'll run out of rice balls!

00:20:52.790 --> 00:20:54.460
First come first served for eggs in <i>oden</i>!

00:20:54.460 --> 00:20:57.790
You know his whereabouts?

00:20:57.790 --> 00:21:00.730
An isolated island in
the Adonia Sea, Kraken.

00:21:00.730 --> 00:21:03.400
Creed Diskenth is there, too.

00:21:03.400 --> 00:21:05.130
Creed is...

00:21:06.070 --> 00:21:08.000
Now he said it...

00:21:10.410 --> 00:21:13.100
A goodnight call to Kuro-<i>sama...</i>

00:21:17.080 --> 00:21:18.410
Hhmmm!

00:21:18.410 --> 00:21:22.480
Kuro-<i>sama</i>, what're you doing!?

00:21:32.090 --> 00:21:33.430
Train!

00:21:33.430 --> 00:21:35.760
So, he's gone...

00:21:35.760 --> 00:21:37.430
To the Apostles of the Stars?

00:21:37.430 --> 00:21:41.440
He's probably thinking that he doesn't
wanna involve us or something anyway.

00:21:41.440 --> 00:21:44.110
He treats us like strangers...

00:21:44.110 --> 00:21:45.770
You're just the same, Sven, aren't you?

00:21:45.770 --> 00:21:46.770
Huh?

00:21:46.770 --> 00:21:52.010
You joined the sweeper alliance secretly...
to catch Creed, right?

00:21:53.110 --> 00:21:55.120
That fool...

00:21:55.120 --> 00:21:58.990
He always leaves his friends behind...

00:22:14.070 --> 00:22:21.070
<i>Since your new black boots</i>
<i>caused a blister,</i>

00:22:21.070 --> 00:22:28.080
<i>you rest your right foot</i>

00:22:28.080 --> 00:22:38.080
<i>We'll keep walking along</i>
<i>with our own rhythm, without rushing</i>

00:22:41.600 --> 00:22:51.590
<i>Don't say anything</i>
<i>because we'll soon understand each other</i>

00:22:56.140 --> 00:23:06.140
<i>I'm just holding you now to keep you warm</i>

00:23:10.390 --> 00:23:20.390
<i>I'm completely wrapped around you, so...</i>

00:23:20.800 --> 00:23:30.800
<i>Quietly the powder-like snow</i>
<i>is building up...</i>

00:23:40.120 --> 00:23:41.090
"Next Episode"

00:23:41.090 --> 00:23:42.420
<i>That darn Train!</i>
"Next Episode"

00:23:42.420 --> 00:23:45.420
<i>Does he intend to settle it</i>
<i>with Creed all by himself?</i>

00:23:46.430 --> 00:23:48.090
<i>I won't let you!</i>

00:23:48.090 --> 00:23:51.770
<i>As if I'd let you have</i>
<i>the starring role all to yourself!</i>

00:23:51.770 --> 00:23:56.290
<i>We'll definitely catch up with you</i>
<i>using my beloved car, so be prepared!</i>

00:23:59.440 --> 00:24:02.380
<i>Oh, hey Rins... sorry, but can</i>
<i>you lend me some money for gas?</i>

00:24:02.380 --> 00:24:03.440
"Dozing Cat"
<i>Oh, hey Rins... sorry, but can</i>
<i>you lend me some money for gas?</i>

00:24:03.440 --> 00:24:05.040
"Dozing Cat"
